\f1\fs22 For a moment, Special Agent Ajent (pronounced 
\f2\i Ar-zhant
\f1\i0 ) Jones reckoned Sarah might just be too good-looking to whack. Even afterwards, fury throbbed through him, burning off all sense, making him forget about the missing disc and the missing blank, Emil Kalheri.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>He should have hit her. The truth was, nothing gave him a bigger kick than messing up a beautiful woman\'92s face. The pretty ones: he loved the look of shock, shattering their smug belief that they could put any bloke in his place, with no more than a glare or a sharp word. We\'92re all just man-boys to them. There was poetry in seeing that delusion crack, the realisation blooming in their bloodied eye sockets that the world\'92s not soft, not fair\'97just rough and honest. He did everyone a favour, really, showing them the truth. It was a public service.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Of course, what he never told anyone\'97not even himself on most days\'97was a dim memory that ever since he was a kid, he ached to please women. Which is why he hated them so much.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>So why\'92d he hold back when she confronted him in Travis Teh\'92s office? When he went at her, she stared him dead in the eye, cocky as you please, condescending smile pasted across her face. That look made him want to smash something. He hated those smiles. They were begging for the back of his hand. So why didn\'92t he wipe it clean off her face?\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>He punched the steering wheel. Then the window. Then the wheel again, trying to silence the pounding behind his eyes.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The still-beautiful computer jockey could hold onto the goods for now\'97the disc, the Gyges Disc\'97what Emil Kalheri should have pulled out of Travis Teh\'92s cold hands. She was clearly Cyber Security (her tits were too small for Finance), so maybe she had her own reasons for chasing the disc. Maybe she was an op, maybe PAPER had thrown a second team at the job. Wouldn\'92t be the first time the Company tried to hedge its bets. He\'92d give her both Pre-emptive Reciprocity and Proactive Euthanasia, make no mistake about that.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>PAPER: Proactive Agency for Pre-emptive Euthanasia and Reciprocity. Typical government-title-speak that was only a thinnest of veneers over the agency\'92s authority to not only kill and ask questions later, but to do its best to argue the questions came first. Its mission both thrilled and chilled Jones. Chilled him pleasurably, almost to completion.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Once he\'92d settled his nerves, he was able to focus on Emil\'92s vanishing act. Maybe Emil took off because he failed with the disc, or maybe Miss Cyber-Security Beauty Queen Bitch stitched him up along with everything else. Either way, Jones would hunt Emil down, quick-smart.
